  <page_number>263</page_number>
  <running_head>EPIGRAM. A. FAYI.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>R iiij</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">unt loco nunquam dociles manere:</l>
    <l n="2">unt foco semper faciles moueri:</l>
    <l n="3">ræpetes semper fugiunt eundo,</l>
    <l n="4">Séque sequendo.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Lydiæ Croesus dominator oræ,Se</l>
    <l n="6">nihil supra positum putabat:</l>
    <l n="7">Parte credebat fieri sed omni-</l>
    <l n="8">Séque beatum.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Temporis puncto superante Cyro-</l>
    <l n="10">Perdit illustris diadema regni,</l>
    <l n="11">Perdit &amp; gazas numero carentes-</l>
    <l n="12">Nudior Iro.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Fictiles fingens Agathoclis ollas-</l>
    <l n="14">Dextra, fit sceptris habilis gerendis,</l>
    <l n="15">Et luti sordes rutilantis auri-</l>
    <l n="16">Pondere mutat.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Rursus est idem folio regali-</l>
    <l n="18">Pulsus: &amp; vitæ miseranda tandem-</l>
    <l n="19">Claustra fortitus: solitâ tyrannis-</l>
    <l n="20">Morte peremptus.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Si quis antiquæ monimenta chartæ-</l>
    <l n="22">Addita charta relegat recente:</l>
    <l n="23">Mille signabit simili lapillo-</l>
    <l n="24">Regia fata.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Cespitem parui tuguri videbit-</l>
    <l n="26">Esse non parui dominantis ortu-</l>
    <l n="27">Nobilem: contrà Pario nitentes-</l>
    <l n="28">Marmore turres.</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">Pauperem magnis genuisse tectis:</l>
    <l n="30">Sceptra cum rastris variata: sicque-</l>
    <l n="31">Esse mortales similes rotarum-</l>
    <l n="32">Mobiliorum.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Some words at the left edge are cut off by the scan (first letters missing, e.g. "unt" for "Sunt"); the faint background text is show-through and was omitted. Words marked as doubtful were not flagged; the transcription follows the printed letters as far as legible.</notes>
</page>
